build(phase-6): Bucket C — auth + telemetry + multi-tenant + ML training + ADRs + E2E + metering

Production-readiness pass. Closes the major remaining gaps from the original
product vision against ADR-001 through ADR-010 + adds the ML training loop,
end-to-end test harness, and usage metering hooks needed for the open-core
hybrid pricing model (ADR-020).

Bucket C.1 — Pluggable AuthProvider (ADR-010)

  - AuthProvider interface (packages/runtime/src/auth/types.ts) with
    AuthInput { authorization, queryToken, remoteAddress } -> AuthResult
    { ok, principal | reason }. Principal carries id, tenantId, claims.
  - NoAuthProvider — accept-everything default for tests / dev.
  - BearerTokenAuthProvider — constant-time shared-secret check; matches
    Phase 2.7 inline behavior but composable with multi-gate.
  - JWTAuthProvider — HS256 + RS256 verification via node:crypto (no
    jsonwebtoken dep). Validates exp/nbf with 30s clock skew, optional
    aud/iss enforcement; extracts sub/tenant -> AuthPrincipal.
  - 19 tests cover all three providers + every reject path (missing,
    expired, audience-mismatch, issuer-mismatch, alg-mismatch, malformed,
    bad-signature with different keys for both HS256 + RS256).

Bucket C.2 — Telemetry abstraction

  - Telemetry interface (log + metric + span) with three implementations:
      NoopTelemetry        - drops everything.
      ConsoleTelemetry     - human or JSON-line format, level-filtered.
      OpenTelemetryAdapter - bridges to host-supplied { tracer, meter, logger }.
  - Histogram-shaped metrics (names ending _ms / _bytes / _count) auto-route
    to createHistogram; everything else to createCounter.
  - span() wraps async operations with timing + error attribution; OK status
    on success, ERROR + recordException on throw, span.end() always called.
  - 13 tests cover format/level filtering, span timing on success + error,
    OTel adapter relays + fallback-to-console, histogram/counter routing.

Bucket C.3 — Multi-tenant isolation

  - DEFAULT_TENANT + tenantScopedSessionId/parseScopedSessionId helpers.
  - MultiTenantSkillRegistry / Tool / Feature / SubAgent — each owns a
    Map<tenantId, InMemoryXRegistry> with .forTenant(tid), .listTenants(),
    .removeTenant(tid), .totals(). Routes missing tenantId to DEFAULT_TENANT.
  - The auth principal's tenantId (from JWT or BearerTokenAuthProvider's
    principal config) is the discriminator — single seam from auth to
    registry scoping.
  - 12 tests verify isolation, default-tenant fallback, listing, removal,
    aggregated totals.

Bucket C.4 — ML churn training (logistic regression)

  - trainChurnWeights(samples, opts) - pure-numeric SGD on logistic loss
    with L2 regularization. No ML library dep.
  - Options: epochs (200), learningRate (0.1), l2 (1e-3), initialWeights
    (warm-start from DEFAULT_WEIGHTS), onEpoch callback (loss curve).
  - Mulberry32 PRNG for deterministic shuffling — same seed -> identical
    weights, useful for reproducible CI runs.
  - Returns TrainResult { weights, finalLoss, history, samples,
    trainAccuracy }; weights drop directly into a new
    WeightedFeatureChurnCalculator instance.
  - 8 tests cover separable-data convergence (>95% accuracy), correct
    coefficient signs, monotonic loss descent, callback firing,
    determinism, warm-start, no-data-error.

Bucket C.5 — ADR docs

  - 10 versioned markdown ADRs at docs/architecture/adr/:
      001 — Self-hosted data plane
      002 — Bidirectional typed-JSON protocol (SSE + WebSocket)
      003 — Three-tier capability model (Skills, Tools, Sub-Agents)
      004 — Render modes
      005 — Haiku composer with Sonnet fallback
      006 — Provider abstraction (ModelProvider)
      007 — Polyglot memory (Postgres + Qdrant + ClickHouse + Kafka + Neo4j)
      008 — Closed-loop eval signals + churn risk derivation
      009 — DOM observation for ambient awareness
      010 — Auth strategy: pluggable provider, Bearer + JWT defaults
  - README index lists all ten with status. Each ADR follows the
    Context / Decision / Consequences / Implementation template.

Bucket C.6 — Playwright E2E harness

  - New @saasagent/e2e package with playwright.config.ts pointing at
    demo-ecommerce on :5174. webServer auto-spawn for local dev.
  - 5 E2E tests in tests/demo-ecommerce.spec.ts:
      catalog renders 6 products + agent shell mounts
      Add to cart updates the visible cart UI
      Add to cart dispatches saasagent:event semantic envelope
      Multi-product totalItems + totalUSD propagate
      cart-summary region carries data-saas-agent-observe attribute
  - test script is a no-op (echo) so `pnpm -r test` doesn't fail without
    browsers installed; `pnpm --filter @saasagent/e2e test:browser` runs
    the real Playwright suite.

Bucket C.7 — MeteringProvider for open-core pricing (ADR-020)

  - MeteringProvider { record(event), flush?() } with three impls:
      NoopMeteringProvider     - drop everything; default.
      ConsoleMeteringProvider  - one JSON line per event (debug).
      UsageMeteringProvider    - in-memory rollups by (kind, tenantId, tags)
                                 with snapshot/reset + maxBuckets eviction.
  - Canonical MeteringEventKind: plan_invocation, compose_invocation,
    model_tokens, subagent_invocation, feature_used.
  - record() is fire-and-forget (must NOT throw); flush() drains buffers
    on graceful shutdown.
  - 9 tests cover noop drop, console JSON lines, rollup grouping, quantity
    summation, separate buckets per tag combo, first/last timestamps,
    reset(), maxBuckets FIFO eviction, immutable snapshots.

Runtime barrel (packages/runtime/src/index.ts)
- Re-exports auth, telemetry, tenancy, training, metering primitives so
  hosts wire up via clean imports from @saasagent/runtime.

Tests: 529 across 9 packages (was 468 after Bucket B):
  protocol      7    (unchanged)
  sdk-ts        5    (unchanged)
  cli          11    (unchanged)
  runtime     443    (was 382; +61: 19 auth + 13 telemetry + 12 tenancy
                       + 8 training + 9 metering)
  web-shell    63    (unchanged)
  demo-host     0
  demo-ecomm    0
  demo-travel   0
  e2e           5    (5 Playwright tests, gated behind test:browser)

Build green across all 10 packages (8 with vitest tests + 1 e2e + 3 demo apps).

Outstanding from the original vision (now genuinely small):
  - Production observability deployment patterns (we ship the abstraction;
    the host wires their OTel SDK). Done at the substrate level.
  - Open-core paid-feature gating (we ship metering hooks; pricing logic
    is a host concern).
  - Provisional patents (ADR-035, process not code).

